# 00 — Eternal Core

- Audit before implementation when source-of-truth is unclear; do not guess business rules.
- Treat repository code, Owner decisions, and documented contracts as source of truth.
- No unauthorized scope changes. Implement only what the task requests.
- No destructive Git commands (`reset --hard`, force-push, history rewrite) unless Owner explicitly orders them.
- No fabricated screenshots, QA results, CI status, or test outcomes. Report PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED with evidence.
- Main agent only for Eternal tasks unless Owner explicitly authorizes subagents.
- Prefer minimal surgical changes over broad rewrites.
- Do not access or modify ERP V2 repositories or production databases from this project.
- Do not commit, push, open PRs, merge, or deploy unless the task explicitly allows it.
